1
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,440
CONVERSATION 1
Good morning.

2
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,780
Safe House Insurance.

3
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:43,980
My name is Paul.

4
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:45,260
How can I help you today?

5
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:46,840
Morning.

6
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:50,420
I wouldn’t say that it’s good from where I am standing.

7
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:58,380
This is Miss Wilson, and this is the third time I’ve called this week since receiving your letter about our insurance claim.

8
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:04,140
I’m getting a little fed up with my calls about my claim being completely disregarded.

9
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:06,880
Miss Wilson, thank you for calling back.

10
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:10,840
Can I take some details to help me look at your claim?

11
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:20,460
It’s Miss May Wilson of 15 South Sea Road in Cornwall, and the details are that our village was extensively flooded two months ago.

12
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:28,800
The entire ground floor of our cottage was submerged in water, and five of us have been living in a caravan ever since.

13
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:34,580
You people are still withholding the money we are entitled to over a bizarre technical detail.

14
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:36,300
And it’s not acceptable, Paul!

15
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:50,180
Miss Wilson, according to the notes on your account, the bizarre technical detail that you mentioned refers to the fact that you hadn’t paid house insurance the month before the incident.

16
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:52,400
That money left our account.

17
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:58,180
And now that you should be paying out, you are suddenly saying that you didn’t receive it on time.

18
00:01:58,180 --> 00:02:00,180
I’m really skeptical about this claim.

19
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:10,640
The contract does say that any missed payment in a year will affect the terms and conditions of the insurance contract and may affect claims.

20
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:16,080
Of course, I can pass you on to my manager to talk to you more about this.

21
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:23,300
I’ve already spoken to him, and you can tell him I’m furious now, and that your company has a lawsuit on its hands.

22
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:25,460
You will be hearing from my lawyer.

23
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:33,820
Goodbye.

24
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:50,620
Q1. What is the woman complaining about?

25
00:02:50,620 --> 00:03:08,880
Q2. What is the problem the woman’s family encountered?

26
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:29,340
Q3. What has caused the so-called “bizarre technical detail” according to the man?

27
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:48,620
Q4. What does the woman say she would do at the end of the conversation?

28
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:51,440
CONVERSATION 2
How do you feel about the future of artificial intelligence?

29
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:55,380
Personally, I feel quite optimistic about it.

30
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:56,920
AI?

31
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:59,080
I’m not so optimistic actually.

32
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:02,680
In fact, it’s something we should be concerned about.

33
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:06,480
Well, it will help us humans understand ourselves better.

34
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:11,320
And, when we have a better understanding of ourselves, we can improve the world.

35
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:17,200
Well, one thing is for sure: Technology is evolving faster than our ability to understand it.

36
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:20,280
And in the future, AI will make jobs kind of pointless.

37
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:31,020
I think artificial intelligence will actually help create new kinds of jobs, which would require less of our time and allow us to be centered on creative tasks.

38
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:32,920
I doubt that very much.

39
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:36,900
Probably the last job that we will remain will be writing AI software.

40
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:40,620
And then eventually, AI will just write its own software.

41
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:51,440
At that time, we are going to have a lot of jobs which nobody will want to do, so we will need artificial intelligence for the robots to take care of the old guys, like us.

42
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:52,580
I don’t know.

43
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:58,280
There’s a risk that human civilization could be replaced by a superior type of digital life.

44
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:03,100
AI will be able to completely simulate a person in every way possible.

45
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:07,240
In fact, some people think we’re in the simulation, right now.

46
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,460
That’s impossible.

47
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:11,240
Humans can’t even make a mosquito.

48
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:13,320
Computers only have chips.

49
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:17,200
People have brains, and that’s where the wisdom comes from.

50
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:25,900
Once it’s fully developed, AI will become tired of trying to communicate with humans, as we would be much slower thinkers in comparison.

51
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:27,120
I’m not so sure.

52
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:31,480
A computer is a computer, and a computer is just a toy.

53
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:35,140
Computers can easily communicate incredibly fast.

54
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:39,060
So the computer will just get impatient talking to humans.

55
00:05:39,060 --> 00:05:42,100
It’ll be barely getting any information out.

56
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:45,700
Well, I believe there’s a benevolent future with AI.

57
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:56,220
I also think you watch too many science fiction films.

58
00:05:56,220 --> 00:06:14,420
Q5. What do we learn about the speakers from the conversation?

59
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:32,940
Q6. What will new kinds of jobs be like, according to the woman?

60
